Commit message:
Fixed bugs in gsMemory and gsStopWatch related to C++98 incompatibilities (#378)

* Declaration of "to-be-deleted" copy assignment and constructor as private does not work on C++98 mode

* Keyword "restrict" should not be used as parameter since it leads to compiler errors with the PGI compiler

* Fixed inconsistent use of boost::shared_prt and boost::weak_ptr with Intel ICC compiler

* Problem fixed: Clang (at least under macOS) defines nullptr in C++98 which leads to an error if it is redefined here

